<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giuseppe Mazzini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a>–<a href="/years/1872">1872</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giuseppe Mazzini was a Genoese revolutionary and founder of Young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, who campaigned for a united, republican Italy. In 1848 he joined the republicans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, and in 1849 he led the triumvirate of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> until French troops restored papal rule. He spent most of his life in exile, and Italy was united as a monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giuseppe-mazzini.jpg" alt="Giuseppe Mazzini" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giuseppe_Mazzini.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
